1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,414
The consequences arrived on every way into the city: the railway, the motorway, the freeway, and the expressway.

2
00:00:07,414 --> 00:00:15,464
After a century of iron and steam, the train had become a tourist attraction and the bus a last resort.

3
00:00:15,464 --> 00:00:24,294
“Our second fleet is a fleet of excuses,” the pilot said, and the crew laughed without much ease.

4
00:00:24,294 --> 00:00:32,809
A commuter on the morning shuttle, a rider with a trailer, and a swimmer from the north all waited in the same lane.

5
00:00:32,809 --> 00:00:43,579
A shipment of dirt, a haul of timber, and a drill for the tunnel: the transport of goods had become more certain than the transport of people.

6
00:00:43,579 --> 00:00:50,064
“We cannot pave a passage with a constitution,” the foreigner said.

7
00:00:50,064 --> 00:00:56,194
The migrant workers watched the flight board with the ease of people who had done it before.

8
00:00:56,194 --> 00:01:15,199
“The railway is a window,” the station master said, “and a window is not a door.” A steamer at the post, a ferry in the bay, and a fleet of fishing boats gave the harbour its roar, but the shipping schedule was still written by hand.

9
00:01:15,199 --> 00:01:22,004
The tourist season brought an excursion, a tour, and a crowd of passengers with cameras.

10
00:01:22,004 --> 00:01:34,699
The runner, the pilot, and the crew of the small aviation club had all signed the offer; the large part of the work, as always, fell on the commuters themselves.

11
00:01:34,699 --> 00:01:44,309
A foreigner with a return ticket and a century of patience asked the only question that mattered: who continues the line?

12
00:01:44,309 --> 00:01:53,753
After the vote, the company continued to run the shuttle and the trailer service, and the importation of spare parts went on.

13
00:01:53,753 --> 00:01:59,178
Behind the station, the crew repaired a wagon with iron and hope.

14
00:01:59,178 --> 00:02:07,183
Our second attempt would follow the same way, and the watch on the platform was the same as the one in the office.

15
00:02:07,183 --> 00:02:16,518
The highway, the expressway, the trunk road, and the railroad all came to the same small nation of travellers.

16
00:02:16,518 --> 00:02:36,022
“It is possible that a national service will never pay,” the pilot said, “and it is certain that a war of schedules will.” The fleet, the freeway, and the freight yard: the whole apparatus of movement was built for goods, and the people came second.
